\f2\b \cf3 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Role in Story:
\f1\b0 	Central Male Character\

\f2\b <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Occupation:
\f1\b0 	Contract Cleaner\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb5 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At the start of the book Cracker is a mere cleaner and neither happy nor unhappy with his existence.\'a0 But meeting Sarah makes him want more - he wants to be treated like the Airborne or at least something along the lines of equal treatment.\'a0 As a cloudborne individual he does not have the capacity to challenge the structures of society so he needs assistance.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf3 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'a0	\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf3 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Physical Description:
\f1\b0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>appearance, 183cm, medium build, dark straight hair, pale complexion, dark slightly hooded eyes, straight-slender nose, bright smile with straight white teeth. Hands calloused, cracked and grimy. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\

\f2\b <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Personality:
\f1\b0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Poorly educated, but intelligent, street-wise and wise cracking. He has a childish and crude sense of humour and regularly makes coarse and inappropriate comments. He will steal anything if there is a prospect of getting away with it, but he is fiercely loyal and would never double-cross a friend. Blend of amoral criminality and Victorian decency.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\

\f2\b <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Habits/Mannerisms:
\f1\b0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Thief, crude comments. Awkward attempts at humour. Loves to High five.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'a0 	\

\f2\b <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Background:
\f1\b0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He was brought up by an uncle who disappeared/abandoned him while he was in his mid teens. He remained in the apartment he was brought up in, expecting eviction that never came. He fell into contract cleaning and started his own company. He uses his contacts in law enforcement to obtain contracts/jobs cleaning crime scenes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\

\f2\b <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Internal Conflicts:
\f1\b0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He hates his station in life and knows he cannot change it. He desperately wants to be loved, but the impersonal nature of the society has made a search for love impossible. He always desires women that are higher born and completely out of reach.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

